# API settings. Copy this file to api/.env (git-ignored) and uncomment what you change: the API, the CLI and the
# MCP server read api/.env wherever they start, and an environment variable of the same name overrides it.
# Each line shows the setting's default, so a copy changes nothing until you edit it.
# api/tests/test_env_example.py keeps this list in step with igneous/config.py.

# ---- Where things are

# Postgres database. The default is the Enron demo database; keep your own data in a separate one, such as
# postgresql+psycopg://igneous:igneous@localhost:5432/igneous_personal (README: "Demo data or your own data").
# IGNEOUS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://igneous:igneous@localhost:5432/igneous
# The Google OAuth client and the token encryption key (google/), the Enron mailboxes (maildir/), the synthetic
# persona (persona/) and, unless IGNEOUS_MODEL_CACHE_DIR names another folder, the local models (models/). A
# relative path is relative to the api folder.
# IGNEOUS_DATA_DIR=../data
# Where the web app runs: the only site whose pages may call the API, and where Google sign-in sends the browser
# back. The API answers to localhost and to this URL's host name, nothing else.
# IGNEOUS_WEB_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---- Sources

# Comma-separated folders the Local files source reads, such as ~/Documents/notes,~/Desktop. Empty reads whichever
# of Documents, Desktop, Downloads and iCloud Drive exist. Name only folders that exist: a missing one stops
# Local files from syncing.
# IGNEOUS_FILESYSTEM_ROOTS=
# Drive API page size for listing files and changes (1-1000).
# IGNEOUS_DRIVE_PAGE_SIZE=100
# Gmail API quota units per minute the connector paces itself to. A Google project in Testing mode is cut off
# near 730; raise it if your project's quota page allows more.
# IGNEOUS_GMAIL_UNITS_PER_MIN=600

# ---- Local models (FastEmbed: no credentials, and no text leaves the machine)

# Embedding model; it must make 384-dimensional vectors (chunks.embedding). Changing it re-embeds every chunk on the
# next pipeline run; a model of another width needs a migration that changes the column.
# IGNEOUS_EMBEDDING_MODEL=BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5
# Chunks embedded per batch.
# IGNEOUS_EMBEDDING_BATCH_SIZE=128
# Folder the embedding and reranker models download into. Empty means <data_dir>/models.
# IGNEOUS_MODEL_CACHE_DIR=
# Ask's cross-encoder scores the retrieved and graph-expanded passages and keeps the best 8; false keeps retrieval
# order with 3 of the 8 places held for graph neighbours.
# IGNEOUS_RERANKER_ENABLED=true
# Cross-encoder model.
# IGNEOUS_RERANKER_MODEL=Xenova/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2
# Passages Ask retrieves for each question, and so the most the cross-encoder scores.
# IGNEOUS_RERANKER_POOL_SIZE=16
# Candidates scored per batch.
# IGNEOUS_RERANK_BATCH_SIZE=64

# ---- Hosted models (Bedrock)

# false turns off every hosted model call: search and the graph keep working, and Ask returns 503.
# IGNEOUS_LLM_ENABLED=true
# Comma-separated source ids (the Sources page shows them) whose records a hosted model may read; empty sends
# nothing. With the Enron demo database: email. With your own: personal ids such as gmail,ai_chats,takeout.
# IGNEOUS_LLM_SOURCES=
# true lets a hosted model read local files and Apple Notes too, when their ids are in IGNEOUS_LLM_SOURCES. Search
# embeds and reranks them on this computer either way.
# IGNEOUS_LOCAL_SOURCES_MODEL_ENABLED=false
# Model for Ask, extraction and nuanced judgments: naming threads, picking their records, confirming a merge.
# IGNEOUS_LLM_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5
# Model for high-volume judgments: verifying links, same-or-related pairs, umbrellas, summaries, and the filters a
# question states when the rules find none.
# IGNEOUS_LLM_CHEAP_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0
# Retries after a connection error, a rate limit or a server error, with backoff (the Anthropic SDK's own; there is
# no other retry layer).
# IGNEOUS_HOSTED_RETRIES=2

# ---- Bedrock credentials
# Not settings: the API, the CLI and the MCP server read these only from their process environment, never from
# this file. Export them in the shell that starts the process; the README's "MCP server" section shows how to pass
# them to the MCP server.
#   export AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=...   your Bedrock API key; without it Ask returns 503 and extraction is skipped
#   export AWS_REGION=us-east-1           the default when unset
